    <blockquote class="inline_help">
        <p>These thresholds control notifications, user actions, dashboard and footer status for the primary network interface. Each row keeps its own threshold, unit and action selections.</p>
        <p>Notifications and user actions require their respective global threshold exceeded or threshold reset switches to be enabled. The Enabled/Disabled label describes the entered limit; it does not enable those global switches.</p>
        <p>Stop Docker and Disconnect VM run when the threshold is exceeded. Start Docker and Reconnect VM run when it returns to normal (reset). Select None to leave that action unconfigured.</p>
        <p>Disconnecting and reconnecting a VM is equivalent to unplugging and replugging its network cable; it does not change the VM configuration.</p>
        <p>For additional commands or advanced scripting, edit <strong>dvm-user-actions.sh</strong> using the DVM configuration editor.</p>
    </blockquote>
